  "phase3_gemini_self_healing": {
    "forensics": "The losing cluster is primarily driven by a unidirectional LONG bias on a single bearish regime day (2026-10-22 accounted for 5 losses) where mid-morning entries (10:30\u201311:10 IST) were repeatedly whipsawed by tight 0.45%\u20130.65% stops inside normal NSE 5-minute volatility noise. Additionally, statutory transaction fees (~0.14% round-trip) turned gross-profitable trades (ICICIBANK trailing stop and COALINDIA late-afternoon EOD square-off) into net losses, while the \u20b947.93 total fee drag consumed nearly 80% of the net loss.",
    "learning": "In NSE cash equities, setting initial stop-losses below 0.60% places orders inside intraday liquidity-sweep zones, while triggering breakeven stops at 1.0R without clearing the ~0.15% round-trip brokerage and STT hurdle guarantees negative expectancy via fee attrition.",
    "parameter_patch": {
